# KEYMAP.md §Dialogs and text inputs — Settings (`,`): "`Enter` saves · `Esc` discards"
#
# Settings is a dialog like any other as far as the key table is concerned: it takes the whole
# keyboard under `Dialog > Settings` and gives it back on `Esc`. This scenario checks the frame
# around it rather than the switches inside it — the dialog host owns the field list, and the
# projection reports `dialog.fields` empty rather than guessing at it
# (`docs/TESTING-HARNESS.md` §3).
fixture: one-repo
await idle 30000
assert screen == Hub && mode == Normal && overlay absent

key ,
await overlay == Dialog 10000
assert mode == Dialog && dialog.name == Settings
assert key_contexts[0] == Dialog && key_contexts[1] == Settings
assert focused == dialog
shot settings
dump settings

# `Esc` discards and restores the Hub exactly as it was.
key escape
await overlay absent
assert screen == Hub && mode == Normal && focused == worktrees.row[0] && dialog absent
dump discarded
quit
